---
import GameLayout from "../../../layouts/GameLayout.astro";
---

<GameLayout title="OverTheWire: Drifter Level 6" gameName="drifter" level={6}>
    <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Level 6 is a simple remote daemon with a particular vulnerability. In
        what I intended for this level, it is running in a vulnerable state :P
    </p>

    <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4 font-bold">Reading material:</p>

    <ul class="list-disc list-inside pl-4 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        <li>
            <a
                href="http://www.phrack.org/archives/59/p59-0x07.txt"
                class="text-neutral-500 hover:text-neutral-300 no-underline"
                >Advances in format string exploitation</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="http://julianor.tripod.com/bc/NN-formats.txt"
                class="text-neutral-500 hover:text-neutral-300 no-underline"
                >Format String Technique</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="http://doc.bughunter.net/format-string/exploit-fs.html"
                class="text-neutral-500 hover:text-neutral-300 no-underline"
                >Exploiting Format String Vulnerabilities</a>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
        As usual when I grab random code and look over it, someone might want to
        tell the developer :P
    </p>
</GameLayout>
